  "description": "BIGVILLE R4 (block 252000) -- LOCAL exchange + credit. `be_exchange` is THE buy decision: a buyer CO-LOCATED with a seller at an OPEN shop (`at_cell`+`is_at` share ONE cell var), the buyer wanting what the shop sells and holding coin>=price, transfers coin<->good and DROPS hunger (clamped at 0). It is LOCAL BY CONSTRUCTION -- the co-location join means a buyer only ever transacts with a shop AT ITS CELL, never a global market-clear (the O(N^2) all-pairs trap the scale gate falsifies). `be_credit` fires when the buyer is SHORT of coin and the seller EXTENDS credit -- a decision_value TRUST = credit_trust - risk_weight*buyer.default_count > 0 (the SAME Argmax/decision family as ss_choose_burn / the R2 preference choice): the good is handed over and an `Owe{amount,due_epoch}` obligation minted (buyer -owes-> Owe -creditor-> keeper). A prior DEFAULT drops the creditor's credit_trust below 0 so TRUST<=0 -> neither rule fires -> NO sale (the 'refuse credit / demand cash' behaviour). Composes existing Terms; zero new Rust.",
