      "comment": "PRICE is marked down by freshness: a stale perishable stock sells for price*condition (fresh/durable = full price; coin still conserved -- buyer pays and keeper receives the SAME discounted amount). A SALE IS BETWEEN TWO PEOPLE, not a stall open by the clock: it needs the buyer and the SELLER (keeper) co-located, the seller CONSCIOUS (not asleep/collapsed -- a world fact), goods, and coin. Business HOURS are a construct (a held expectation, be_shop_open + the expectation rule), NOT a world-fact gate on the physical exchange -- two present, conscious people can trade whenever. THE PRICE IS THE SELLER'S: the engine transfers shop.price exactly (a person set it), it does not compute price from freshness -- a seller marking down stale goods is the SELLER's pricing decision, not an engine multiply. Integer prices in, integer coin out (fixed precision). (A purchase moves coin<->good into the bag only; it does NOT feed -- EATING relieves hunger, bd_meal_feeds. Buying and eating are different acts.)"
